IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-seat`

-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173) -- CASES FOR THE SEAT LAYER.
-- One group per question of spr-seat.l4, with the facts a real person in the seat would
-- state. Expected values are decided from the text of the regulation named beside each
-- case, before running; none is copied from the encoding's own output.

§ `Cases for the seat questions`

§§ `Do these Regulations apply to me?`

-- Q1. Do these Regulations apply to me (reg 1(3))?
-- Reaching State Pension age on 6 April 2016 is not before it, so the Regulations apply.
#ASSERT `Do these Regulations apply to me` (YMD 2016 4 6)
-- Reaching it on 5 April 2016 is before 6 April 2016: they do not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do these Regulations apply to me` (YMD 2016 4 5))
-- A later date: they apply.
#ASSERT `Do these Regulations apply to me` (YMD 2040 1 1)
-- An earlier date: they do not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do these Regulations apply to me` (YMD 1990 1 1))

-- Q2. Does the benefit I get count as graduated retirement benefit (reg 1(4))?
-- Section 36.
#ASSERT `Does the benefit I get count as graduated retirement benefit` `a benefit under section 36 of the 1965 Act`
-- Section 37 (widows).
#ASSERT `Does the benefit I get count as graduated retirement benefit` `a benefit under section 37 of the 1965 Act`
-- Any other provision.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the benefit I get count as graduated retirement benefit` `a benefit under another provision`)

-- Q3. Are my spouse or civil partner and I treated as married or civil partners at that time (reg 1(5))?
-- Married, neither married to a third person.
#ASSERT `Are my spouse or civil partner and I treated as married or civil partners at that time` `married to each other` FALSE
-- Married, one of them married to a third person: treated as not married to each other.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my spouse or civil partner and I treated as married or civil partners at that time` `married to each other` TRUE)
-- Civil partners, one of them married to a third person: paragraph (5) speaks only of marriage, so the civil partnership stands (F9).
#ASSERT `Are my spouse or civil partner and I treated as married or civil partners at that time` `civil partners of each other` TRUE
-- Civil partners, no third person.
#ASSERT `Are my spouse or civil partner and I treated as married or civil partners at that time` `civil partners of each other` FALSE

-- Q4. What is the full weekly rate of the State Pension, in pounds (reg 1A)?
-- The figure the text gives.
#ASSERT `What is the full weekly rate of the State Pension, in pounds` EQUALS 241.30


§§ `If I am in prison or on remand`

-- Q5. Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody (regs 2, 3)?
-- Imprisoned in Great Britain after conviction: withheld.
#ASSERT `Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody` (YMD 2027 1 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 6 30) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other sentence` FALSE FALSE
-- Not in custody at all: not withheld.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody` (YMD 2027 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 6 30) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other sentence` FALSE FALSE)
-- Remanded in custody, no sentence yet: reg 3(1) lifts reg 2(1), so it is paid.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody` (YMD 2027 1 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 6 30) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `any other sentence` FALSE FALSE)
-- Remanded, then sentenced to imprisonment: reg 2(1) applies after all.
#ASSERT `Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody` (YMD 2027 1 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 6 30) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings` FALSE FALSE
-- Remanded, then sentenced outside Great Britain to a sentence that would not have been imposed here: not a described sentence (reg 3(3)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody` (YMD 2027 1 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 6 30) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings` TRUE TRUE)
-- Unlawfully at large: withheld.
#ASSERT `Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody` (YMD 2027 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 6 30) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other sentence` FALSE FALSE
-- Detained in hospital under section 47, on the day the Secretary of State certified as the release date: withheld (on or before).
#ASSERT `Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody` (YMD 2027 6 30) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 6 30) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other sentence` FALSE FALSE
-- The day after the certified release date: no longer withheld.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody` (YMD 2027 7 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 6 30) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other sentence` FALSE FALSE)
-- Detained under section 47 with no certified release date: the condition is met (fork F5).
#ASSERT `Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody` (YMD 2027 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2027 6 30) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other sentence` FALSE FALSE
-- Imprisoned outside Great Britain where, in similar circumstances here, the person would not have been a prisoner (reg 2(3)): not withheld.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody` (YMD 2027 1 1) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 6 30) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `any other sentence` FALSE FALSE)
-- Detained under the Scottish Act, section 136, in Great Britain: withheld.
#ASSERT `Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody` (YMD 2027 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 6 30) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any other sentence` FALSE FALSE


§§ `If my late spouse or civil partner deferred their State Pension: my choice of a lump sum or a pension (regs 4 to 6)`

-- Q6. Is my choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension made in time (reg 4)?
-- Notice dated 15 January 2027: the three months end on 14 April 2027, so a choice on that day is in time.
#ASSERT `Is my choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension made in time` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 1 15) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2010 3 1) (YMD 2027 4 14) EQUALS `the choice is within the period`
-- A choice on 15 April 2027 is one day late.
#ASSERT `Is my choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension made in time` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 1 15) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2010 3 1) (YMD 2027 4 15) EQUALS `the choice is outside the period`
-- No notice: the period starts on the later of the claim (1 March 2027) and the death (1 March 2010); a choice on the claim day is in time.
#ASSERT `Is my choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension made in time` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2027 1 15) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2010 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS `the choice is within the period`
-- No notice and a choice made before the claim: before the period starts.
#ASSERT `Is my choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension made in time` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2027 1 15) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2010 3 1) (YMD 2027 2 28) EQUALS `the choice is outside the period`
-- Section 8(1) does not apply to the person: regulation 4 does not cover them.
#ASSERT `Is my choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension made in time` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2027 1 15) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2010 3 1) (YMD 2027 4 14) EQUALS `regulation 4 does not cover the person`

-- Q7. May I still make a late choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension (reg 4(4))?
-- All four met.
#ASSERT `May I still make a late choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A lump sum was paid and not repaid in full.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I still make a late choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Nothing was paid, so there is nothing to repay (fork F11).
#ASSERT `May I still make a late choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The Secretary of State does not consider it reasonable.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I still make a late choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Repaid in full but in a different currency.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I still make a late choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- Q8. How much lump sum am I paid if I make a late choice of a survivor's pension, in pounds (reg 4(5))?
-- A late choice of a pension: nil.
#ASSERT `How much lump sum am I paid if I make a late choice of a survivor's pension, in pounds` 3500 TRUE EQUALS 0
-- Not a late choice of a pension: unchanged.
#ASSERT `How much lump sum am I paid if I make a late choice of a survivor's pension, in pounds` 3500 FALSE EQUALS 3500

-- Q9. Do I make my choice in the manner the Regulations require (reg 5)?
-- In writing to the specified office.
#ASSERT `Do I make my choice in the manner the Regulations require` TRUE `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- By telephone to the specified number.
#ASSERT `Do I make my choice in the manner the Regulations require` TRUE `by telephone to a number specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- By telephone where the Secretary of State directed writing.
#ASSERT `Do I make my choice in the manner the Regulations require` TRUE `by telephone to a number specified in writing by the Secretary of State` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In another manner.
#ASSERT `Do I make my choice in the manner the Regulations require` TRUE `in another manner` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Section 8(1) does not apply: the regulation says nothing.
#ASSERT `Do I make my choice in the manner the Regulations require` FALSE `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q10. May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension (regs 6(1), 18(7))?
-- Applying within three months of the notification, in writing, to change to a pension, nothing paid: allowed.
#ASSERT `May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a state pension` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 10000 12000 FALSE FALSE
-- Notification dated 15 January 2027: an application on 14 April 2027 is the last day of the three months.
#ASSERT `May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 4 14) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a state pension` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 10000 12000 FALSE FALSE
-- An application on 15 April 2027 is late.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 4 15) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a state pension` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 10000 12000 FALSE FALSE)
-- A longer period allowed to 30 September 2027 and an application on 1 September 2027.
#ASSERT `May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 9 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) TRUE (YMD 2027 9 30) `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a state pension` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 10000 12000 FALSE FALSE
-- Change to a pension after a lump sum was paid and not repaid: not allowed.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a state pension` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 10000 12000 FALSE FALSE)
-- Lump sum paid, repaid in full in the same currency on 20 February 2027, within the period: allowed.
#ASSERT `May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a state pension` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 2 20) TRUE 10000 12000 FALSE FALSE
-- Lump sum repaid in full in time, but in another currency.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a state pension` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 10000 12000 FALSE FALSE)
-- Change to a lump sum when the pension paid would be less than the lump sum: allowed.
#ASSERT `May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a lump sum` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 10000 12000 FALSE FALSE
-- Change to a lump sum when the pension paid would not be less than the lump sum.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a lump sum` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 12000 12000 FALSE FALSE)
-- By telephone where the Secretary of State directed writing.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `by telephone to a number specified in writing by the Secretary of State` TRUE `a state pension` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 10000 12000 FALSE FALSE)
-- By telephone where writing was not directed.
#ASSERT `May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `by telephone to a number specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a state pension` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 10000 12000 FALSE FALSE
-- A previous alteration for the same deferral.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a state pension` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 10000 12000 TRUE FALSE)
-- Choice treated as made after a death under the 1987 Regulations.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a state pension` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 10000 12000 FALSE TRUE)
-- No application.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE `a state pension` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE 10000 12000 FALSE FALSE)

-- Q11. By when must I apply to change my choice (reg 6(2)(c))?
-- No longer period: three months from 15 January 2027 end on 14 April 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to change my choice` (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 4 14)
-- A longer period to 30 September 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to change my choice` (YMD 2027 1 15) TRUE (YMD 2027 9 30) EQUALS (YMD 2027 9 30)
-- A 'longer' period that ends earlier than the three months does not shorten it.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to change my choice` (YMD 2027 1 15) TRUE (YMD 2027 2 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 4 14)

-- Q12. Have I repaid my lump sum as the Regulations require before I change to a survivor's pension (reg 6(2)(e))?
-- Changing to a pension, nothing was paid: nothing to repay.
#ASSERT `Have I repaid my lump sum as the Regulations require before I change to a survivor's pension` `a state pension` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1)
-- Paid, repaid in full in the same currency on 20 February 2027, within the period ending 14 April 2027.
#ASSERT `Have I repaid my lump sum as the Regulations require before I change to a survivor's pension` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 2 20) TRUE (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1)
-- Paid, repaid in full but only on 15 April 2027, after the period.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I repaid my lump sum as the Regulations require before I change to a survivor's pension` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 4 15) TRUE (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1))
-- Paid and not repaid.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I repaid my lump sum as the Regulations require before I change to a survivor's pension` `a state pension` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1))
-- Changing to a lump sum: the repayment condition does not arise.
#ASSERT `Have I repaid my lump sum as the Regulations require before I change to a survivor's pension` `a lump sum` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2027 2 20) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1)

-- Q13. Is the State Pension I have been paid treated as paid on account of my lump sum (reg 6(3))?
-- Changing to a lump sum, pension paid 10000 against a lump sum of 12000.
#ASSERT `Is the State Pension I have been paid treated as paid on account of my lump sum` `a lump sum` 10000 12000
-- Pension paid not less than the lump sum.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the State Pension I have been paid treated as paid on account of my lump sum` `a lump sum` 12000 12000)
-- Changing to a pension: paragraph (3) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the State Pension I have been paid treated as paid on account of my lump sum` `a state pension` 10000 12000)


§§ `If I put off claiming my own State Pension (regs 7 to 12A)`

-- Q14. Have I validly opted to suspend my State Pension (reg 7)?
-- Entitled, notice in writing.
#ASSERT `Have I validly opted to suspend my State Pension` TRUE TRUE `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE
-- Entitled, notice by telephone.
#ASSERT `Have I validly opted to suspend my State Pension` TRUE TRUE `by telephone to a number specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE
-- By telephone where writing was directed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I validly opted to suspend my State Pension` TRUE TRUE `by telephone to a number specified in writing by the Secretary of State` TRUE)
-- Notice given in another manner.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I validly opted to suspend my State Pension` TRUE TRUE `in another manner` FALSE)
-- Not yet entitled.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I validly opted to suspend my State Pension` FALSE TRUE `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE)
-- No notice given.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I validly opted to suspend my State Pension` TRUE FALSE `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State` FALSE)

-- Q15. Is the date I picked for my suspension to start one the Regulations allow (reg 8(2))?
-- The same day.
#ASSERT `Is the date I picked for my suspension to start one the Regulations allow` (YMD 2027 5 1) (YMD 2027 5 1)
-- The day before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the date I picked for my suspension to start one the Regulations allow` (YMD 2027 5 1) (YMD 2027 4 30))
-- The twenty-eighth day, counting the first as day 1.
#ASSERT `Is the date I picked for my suspension to start one the Regulations allow` (YMD 2027 5 1) (YMD 2027 5 28)
-- The next day, 29 May.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the date I picked for my suspension to start one the Regulations allow` (YMD 2027 5 1) (YMD 2027 5 29))

-- Q16. From what date does my suspension take effect (reg 8)?
-- No date picked: the day the option was exercised.
#ASSERT `From what date does my suspension take effect` (YMD 2027 5 1) FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 5 1)
-- A date picked within 28 days.
#ASSERT `From what date does my suspension take effect` (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 5 10) EQUALS (YMD 2027 5 10)
-- A date picked beyond 28 days is not accepted: the exercise day.
#ASSERT `From what date does my suspension take effect` (YMD 2027 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 6 30) EQUALS (YMD 2027 5 1)

-- Q17. Can I cancel my suspension for this past period (reg 9)?
-- A period exactly 12 months back, ending the day before the claim.
#ASSERT `Can I cancel my suspension for this past period` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 6 15) (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2027 6 14)
-- Starting a day earlier than 12 months back.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I cancel my suspension for this past period` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 6 15) (YMD 2026 6 14) (YMD 2027 6 14))
-- Ending on the day of the claim: not a past period.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I cancel my suspension for this past period` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 6 15) (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2027 6 15))
-- No claim while suspended.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I cancel my suspension for this past period` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2027 6 15) (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2027 6 14))
-- A part of the past period.
#ASSERT `Can I cancel my suspension for this past period` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2027 6 15) (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 3 31)

-- Q18. How far back can I cancel my suspension (reg 9(3))?
-- Cancelling on 15 June 2027.
#ASSERT `How far back can I cancel my suspension` (YMD 2027 6 15) EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 15)

-- Q19. Is this day left out of the days counted towards my deferral (reg 11)?
-- Received universal credit that day.
#ASSERT `Is this day left out of the days counted towards my deferral` TRUE `universal credit` FALSE `income support` FALSE FALSE
-- Nothing of the kind.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day left out of the days counted towards my deferral` FALSE `income support` FALSE `income support` FALSE FALSE)
-- A housemate received an increase of carer's allowance for the person.
#ASSERT `Is this day left out of the days counted towards my deferral` FALSE `income support` TRUE `a carer's allowance` TRUE FALSE
-- Someone received an increase but is neither a spouse, a civil partner nor a housemate.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day left out of the days counted towards my deferral` FALSE `income support` TRUE `a carer's allowance` FALSE FALSE)
-- A prisoner who would not have been paid.
#ASSERT `Is this day left out of the days counted towards my deferral` FALSE `income support` FALSE `income support` FALSE TRUE

-- Q20. How many whole weeks count towards my deferral (reg 12)?
-- 14 days, none left out.
#ASSERT `How many whole weeks count towards my deferral` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 14) 0 EQUALS JUST 2
-- 14 days, 1 left out: 13 days is a part week, counted as a whole week.
#ASSERT `How many whole weeks count towards my deferral` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 14) 1 EQUALS JUST 2
-- 14 days, 7 left out.
#ASSERT `How many whole weeks count towards my deferral` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 14) 7 EQUALS JUST 1
-- 14 days, 8 left out: 6 days is a part week.
#ASSERT `How many whole weeks count towards my deferral` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 14) 8 EQUALS JUST 1
-- 14 days, all 14 left out.
#ASSERT `How many whole weeks count towards my deferral` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 14) 14 EQUALS JUST 0
-- More days left out than the period has.
#ASSERT `How many whole weeks count towards my deferral` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 14) 15 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q21. By how much is my weekly State Pension increased for the weeks I deferred, in pounds (reg 10)?
-- 9 weeks against a rate of 200: 9 x 200 / 900.
#ASSERT `By how much is my weekly State Pension increased for the weeks I deferred, in pounds` 9 200 EQUALS 2
-- One week against 900.
#ASSERT `By how much is my weekly State Pension increased for the weeks I deferred, in pounds` 1 900 EQUALS 1
-- No weeks.
#ASSERT `By how much is my weekly State Pension increased for the weeks I deferred, in pounds` 0 900 EQUALS 0

-- Q22. Does regulation 12A change my increase because my weekly State Pension would have changed during my deferral (reg 12A(1))?
-- A change in the middle of the deferral.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 12A change my increase because my weekly State Pension would have changed during my deferral` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 12 31) TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1)
-- A change on the first day of the deferral.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 12A change my increase because my weekly State Pension would have changed during my deferral` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 12 31) TRUE (YMD 2027 1 1)
-- A change after the deferral ended.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 12A change my increase because my weekly State Pension would have changed during my deferral` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 12 31) TRUE (YMD 2028 1 1))
-- No change.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 12A change my increase because my weekly State Pension would have changed during my deferral` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2027 12 31) FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1))

-- Q23. What is my increment for a period in which my weekly State Pension would not have changed, in pounds (reg 12A(2))?
-- 10 weeks against 900.
#ASSERT `What is my increment for a period in which my weekly State Pension would not have changed, in pounds` 10 900 EQUALS 10
-- 9 weeks against 200.
#ASSERT `What is my increment for a period in which my weekly State Pension would not have changed, in pounds` 9 200 EQUALS 2


§§ `Do I have enough qualifying years? (reg 13)`

-- Q24. Do I have enough qualifying years for this State Pension (reg 13)?
-- Reduced rate, 10 years.
#ASSERT `Do I have enough qualifying years for this State Pension` `a state pension at the reduced rate` 10 EQUALS `the person has enough qualifying years`
-- Reduced rate, 9 years.
#ASSERT `Do I have enough qualifying years for this State Pension` `a state pension at the reduced rate` 9 EQUALS `the person does not have enough qualifying years`
-- Transitional rate, 10 years.
#ASSERT `Do I have enough qualifying years for this State Pension` `a state pension at the transitional rate` 10 EQUALS `the person has enough qualifying years`
-- Transitional rate, 9 years.
#ASSERT `Do I have enough qualifying years for this State Pension` `a state pension at the transitional rate` 9 EQUALS `the person does not have enough qualifying years`
-- Full rate: the Regulations are silent, and say so.
#ASSERT `Do I have enough qualifying years for this State Pension` `a state pension at the full rate` 35 EQUALS `these Regulations do not set the number of qualifying years for this rate`


§§ `If my pension rights are shared on divorce or the end of a civil partnership (regulation 14 and the Schedule)`

-- Q25. What information must the Secretary of State give about my pension rights when sharing is considered (inserted reg 6(1))?
-- I ask.
#ASSERT `What information must the Secretary of State give about my pension rights when sharing is considered` `the person who has shareable new state scheme rights` EQUALS `the information in paragraphs (2) to (6)`
-- The court orders it.
#ASSERT `What information must the Secretary of State give about my pension rights when sharing is considered` `the court, by an order` EQUALS `the information in paragraphs (2) to (6)`
-- My spouse or civil partner asks.
#ASSERT `What information must the Secretary of State give about my pension rights when sharing is considered` `the spouse or civil partner of the person who has shareable new state scheme rights` EQUALS `the information in paragraph (6) only`

-- Q26. Which valuation of my pension rights will I be given (inserted reg 6(2) to (4))?
-- No relevant date: as at the date of receipt.
#ASSERT `Which valuation of my pension rights will I be given` FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 5) EQUALS JUST `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the date the request is received`
-- A relevant date on 6 April 2016 or later.
#ASSERT `Which valuation of my pension rights will I be given` TRUE (YMD 2016 4 6) (YMD 2027 1 5) EQUALS JUST `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the relevant date`
-- A relevant date before 6 April 2016, request received after it.
#ASSERT `Which valuation of my pension rights will I be given` TRUE (YMD 2016 4 5) (YMD 2027 1 5) EQUALS JUST `a valuation of the previous shareable old state scheme rights as at the relevant date`
-- A request received before 6 April 2016: not covered.
#ASSERT `Which valuation of my pension rights will I be given` FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2016 4 5) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q27. May I be given the amount of my former Category A retirement pension (inserted reg 6(5))?
-- Relevant date before 6 April 2016, request received after.
#ASSERT `May I be given the amount of my former Category A retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 2015 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 5)
-- Relevant date on or after 6 April 2016.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I be given the amount of my former Category A retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 2016 4 6) (YMD 2027 1 5))
-- No relevant date.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I be given the amount of my former Category A retirement pension` FALSE (YMD 2015 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 5))
-- Request received before 6 April 2016.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I be given the amount of my former Category A retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 2015 1 1) (YMD 2016 4 5))

-- Q28. By when must the Secretary of State give me the information that has been asked for (inserted reg 6(7), (8))?
-- I ask for a valuation, received 5 January 2027: three months end on 4 April 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must the Secretary of State give me the information that has been asked for` `the person who has shareable new state scheme rights` (YMD 2027 1 5) TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 4 4)
-- The same, having notified that proceedings have begun: six weeks end on 15 February 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must the Secretary of State give me the information that has been asked for` `the person who has shareable new state scheme rights` (YMD 2027 1 5) TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 2 15)
-- The court orders a valuation and sets a shorter period ending 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must the Secretary of State give me the information that has been asked for` `the court, by an order` (YMD 2027 1 5) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 3 1)
-- A court period later than the three months does not extend them.
#ASSERT `By when must the Secretary of State give me the information that has been asked for` `the court, by an order` (YMD 2027 1 5) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2027 6 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 4 4)
-- A shorter period in the input for a request by me is ignored: only a court's order can set one.
#ASSERT `By when must the Secretary of State give me the information that has been asked for` `the person who has shareable new state scheme rights` (YMD 2027 1 5) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 4 4)
-- My spouse or civil partner asks for the explanation: one month, ending 4 February 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must the Secretary of State give me the information that has been asked for` `the spouse or civil partner of the person who has shareable new state scheme rights` (YMD 2027 1 5) TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 2 4)
-- My request includes no valuation or amount: one month.
#ASSERT `By when must the Secretary of State give me the information that has been asked for` `the person who has shareable new state scheme rights` (YMD 2027 1 5) FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 2 4)

-- Q29. Is the valuation I am given calculated and verified on the Government Actuary's guidance (inserted reg 7)?
-- Made.
#ASSERT `Is the valuation I am given calculated and verified on the Government Actuary's guidance` TRUE FALSE
-- In contemplation.
#ASSERT `Is the valuation I am given calculated and verified on the Government Actuary's guidance` FALSE TRUE
-- Neither.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the valuation I am given calculated and verified on the Government Actuary's guidance` FALSE FALSE)


§§ `If my husband, wife or civil partner has died: my inherited pension (regs 15 to 20)`

-- Q30. Which paragraph of regulation 16 gives me an inherited amount (reg 16)?
-- Spouse died 1 March 2010, I reach pensionable age 1 January 2020 and have not married again: paragraph (1).
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of regulation 16 gives me an inherited amount` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) EQUALS JUST `regulation 16(1) applies`
-- Spouse reached pensionable age 1 January 2010 and died 1 June 2016, I am under pensionable age: paragraph (2).
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of regulation 16 gives me an inherited amount` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2016 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2010 1 1) EQUALS JUST `regulation 16(2) applies`
-- The same, but I reached pensionable age on 1 May 2016, before they died: paragraph (3).
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of regulation 16 gives me an inherited amount` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2016 5 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2016 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2010 1 1) EQUALS JUST `regulation 16(3) applies`
-- I married again before reaching pensionable age (spouse died 2010): none.
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of regulation 16 gives me an inherited amount` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) TRUE (YMD 2005 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Spouse reached pensionable age on 6 April 2016, not before it, and died 1 June 2016: none.
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of regulation 16 gives me an inherited amount` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2016 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2016 4 6) EQUALS NOTHING
-- My spouse died on the day I reached pensionable age: neither under nor over it (F20).
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of regulation 16 gives me an inherited amount` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2010 3 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q31. On what date is the rate of my late spouse's or civil partner's benefit fixed (reg 16(6))?
-- Paragraph (1): the date I reach pensionable age.
#ASSERT `On what date is the rate of my late spouse's or civil partner's benefit fixed` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)
-- Paragraph (3): the date my spouse died.
#ASSERT `On what date is the rate of my late spouse's or civil partner's benefit fixed` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2016 5 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2016 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2010 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2016 6 1)
-- No paragraph applies.
#ASSERT `On what date is the rate of my late spouse's or civil partner's benefit fixed` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) TRUE (YMD 2005 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q32. How much a week is my inherited amount, in pounds (reg 16(4))?
-- A weekly rate of 10.
#ASSERT `How much a week is my inherited amount, in pounds` 10 EQUALS 5
-- A weekly rate of 10.50.
#ASSERT `How much a week is my inherited amount, in pounds` 10.50 EQUALS 5.25

-- Q33. Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit (reg 15(2))?
-- All four conditions met.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) (YMD 1990 6 1)
-- Married on 5 April 2016: before 6 April 2016.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) (YMD 2016 4 5)
-- Married on 6 April 2016: not before it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) (YMD 2016 4 6))
-- I have not yet reached pensionable age on the day I ask about.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (YMD 2019 12 31) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) (YMD 1990 6 1))
-- The day I reach pensionable age counts.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) (YMD 1990 6 1)
-- Either of us was married to a third person: treated as not married (reg 1(5)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) (YMD 1990 6 1))
-- Civil partners where one was married to a third person: reg 1(5) speaks of marriage only (F9).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `civil partners of each other` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) (YMD 1990 6 1)
-- My spouse did not die while we were married.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) (YMD 1990 6 1))
-- No inherited amount (I married again before pensionable age).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) TRUE (YMD 2005 1 1) (YMD 1990 6 1))

-- Q34. What weekly rate of survivor's State Pension do I get under regulation 15, in pounds (reg 15(3))?
-- Paragraph (1), benefit 10 a week: half.
#ASSERT `What weekly rate of survivor's State Pension do I get under regulation 15, in pounds` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) 10 EQUALS JUST 5
-- No inherited amount.
#ASSERT `What weekly rate of survivor's State Pension do I get under regulation 15, in pounds` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) TRUE (YMD 2005 1 1) 10 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A spouse who paid no graduated contributions (a rate of 0): paragraph (1)'s condition is not tested (F37), so the rate is nil, not NOTHING.
#ASSERT `What weekly rate of survivor's State Pension do I get under regulation 15, in pounds` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2005 1 1) 0 EQUALS JUST 0

-- Q35. By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week (reg 17)?
-- My other pension already reaches the full rate; an order of 5% comes in: 5% of 10.
#ASSERT `By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week` 10 100 100 FALSE 0 TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST 0.5
-- The same, with only the full rate increased and no order: nothing.
#ASSERT `By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week` 10 100 100 TRUE 10 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- R+S is below the full rate and it goes up 10%: 10% of 10.
#ASSERT `By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week` 10 50 100 TRUE 10 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 1
-- R+S exactly the full rate: still the first case.
#ASSERT `By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week` 50 50 100 TRUE 10 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 5
-- R+S below the full rate and only an order: nothing.
#ASSERT `By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week` 10 50 100 FALSE 0 TRUE 5 EQUALS NOTHING
-- R+S exactly the full rate and only an order: still nothing, not an excess of nil.
#ASSERT `By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week` 50 50 100 FALSE 0 TRUE 5 EQUALS NOTHING
-- R+S above the full rate: 10% of the shortfall (100 - 50).
#ASSERT `By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week` 60 50 100 TRUE 10 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 5
-- R+S above the full rate: 5% of the excess (110 - 100).
#ASSERT `By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week` 60 50 100 FALSE 0 TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST 0.5
-- Both happen: 5 and 0.5 add.
#ASSERT `By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week` 60 50 100 TRUE 10 TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST 5.5
-- Both happen, but R+S is below the full rate: only the full-rate percentage has a paragraph; the order's percentage has none (finding 7).
#ASSERT `By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week` 10 50 100 TRUE 10 TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST 1
-- Neither happens.
#ASSERT `By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week` 60 50 100 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q36. Am I entitled to choose between a lump sum and a State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred benefit (reg 18(1), (8))?
-- Deferred at death and throughout, no section 8(2) choice.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to choose between a lump sum and a State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- I already have a section 8(2) choice: regulation 18(8).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to choose between a lump sum and a State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Not deferred at death.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to choose between a lump sum and a State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Deferred at death but not throughout the 12 months.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to choose between a lump sum and a State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- I married again before reaching pensionable age.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to choose between a lump sum and a State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- I was over pensionable age when they died: marrying again does not matter.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to choose between a lump sum and a State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2016 5 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2016 6 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- They died on the day I reached pensionable age: neither under nor over it (F20).
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to choose between a lump sum and a State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred benefit` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2010 3 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- I have not yet reached pensionable age on the day I ask about.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to choose between a lump sum and a State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred benefit` (YMD 2019 12 31) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- Q37. On what date do I become entitled to make that choice (reg 18(1))?
-- They died long before I reached pensionable age.
#ASSERT `On what date do I become entitled to make that choice` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE EQUALS (YMD 2020 1 1)
-- I reached pensionable age before they died.
#ASSERT `On what date do I become entitled to make that choice` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2016 5 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2016 6 1) FALSE EQUALS (YMD 2016 6 1)

-- Q38. Which date is read as the date I became entitled when my lump sum is worked out (reg 19(2))?
-- They died long before I reached pensionable age.
#ASSERT `Which date is read as the date I became entitled when my lump sum is worked out` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE EQUALS (YMD 2020 1 1)
-- I reached pensionable age before they died.
#ASSERT `Which date is read as the date I became entitled when my lump sum is worked out` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2016 5 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2016 6 1) FALSE EQUALS (YMD 2016 6 1)

-- Q39. Is my choice under regulation 18 made in time (reg 18(4))?
-- Notice dated 15 January 2027: a choice on 14 April 2027 is the last day.
#ASSERT `Is my choice under regulation 18 made in time` TRUE (YMD 2027 1 15) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2027 4 14) EQUALS `the choice is within the period`
-- A choice on 15 April 2027 is late.
#ASSERT `Is my choice under regulation 18 made in time` TRUE (YMD 2027 1 15) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2027 4 15) EQUALS `the choice is outside the period`
-- No notice: the period runs from the later of my claim and their death, to my choice.
#ASSERT `Is my choice under regulation 18 made in time` FALSE (YMD 2027 1 15) (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 3 1) FALSE (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS `the choice is within the period`

-- Q40. May I still make a late choice under regulation 18 (reg 18(4))?
-- All four met.
#ASSERT `May I still make a late choice under regulation 18` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A lump sum was paid and not repaid in full.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I still make a late choice under regulation 18` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Nothing was paid (fork F11).
#ASSERT `May I still make a late choice under regulation 18` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The Secretary of State does not consider it reasonable.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I still make a late choice under regulation 18` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- Q41. How much lump sum am I paid if I make a late choice of a State Pension under regulation 18, in pounds (reg 18(6))?
-- A late choice of a State Pension: nil.
#ASSERT `How much lump sum am I paid if I make a late choice of a State Pension under regulation 18, in pounds` 3500 TRUE EQUALS 0
-- Otherwise unchanged.
#ASSERT `How much lump sum am I paid if I make a late choice of a State Pension under regulation 18, in pounds` 3500 FALSE EQUALS 3500

-- Q42. Am I paid a lump sum or a State Pension under regulation 18 (reg 18(2), (5), (9) to (11))?
-- I chose a lump sum in time.
#ASSERT `Am I paid a lump sum or a State Pension under regulation 18` TRUE TRUE `a lump sum` TRUE FALSE `a lump sum` FALSE EQUALS `a lump sum under regulation 19`
-- I chose a State Pension in time.
#ASSERT `Am I paid a lump sum or a State Pension under regulation 18` TRUE TRUE `a state pension` TRUE FALSE `a lump sum` FALSE EQUALS `a state pension under regulation 20`
-- I made no choice: a lump sum.
#ASSERT `Am I paid a lump sum or a State Pension under regulation 18` TRUE FALSE `a lump sum` FALSE FALSE `a lump sum` FALSE EQUALS `a lump sum under regulation 19`
-- I chose a State Pension, but too late: a lump sum.
#ASSERT `Am I paid a lump sum or a State Pension under regulation 18` TRUE TRUE `a state pension` FALSE FALSE `a lump sum` FALSE EQUALS `a lump sum under regulation 19`
-- I chose a lump sum, then changed to a State Pension, and the change was allowed.
#ASSERT `Am I paid a lump sum or a State Pension under regulation 18` TRUE TRUE `a lump sum` TRUE TRUE `a state pension` TRUE EQUALS `a state pension under regulation 20`
-- I chose a State Pension and asked to change to a lump sum, but the change was refused.
#ASSERT `Am I paid a lump sum or a State Pension under regulation 18` TRUE TRUE `a state pension` TRUE TRUE `a lump sum` FALSE EQUALS `a state pension under regulation 20`
-- Paragraph (1) does not apply to me: not covered.
#ASSERT `Am I paid a lump sum or a State Pension under regulation 18` FALSE TRUE `a state pension` TRUE FALSE `a lump sum` FALSE EQUALS `regulation 18 does not cover the person`

-- Q43. How much lump sum am I paid under regulation 19, in pounds (reg 19(1))?
-- A lump sum under regulation 19.
#ASSERT `How much lump sum am I paid under regulation 19, in pounds` `a lump sum under regulation 19` 3500 EQUALS JUST 3500
-- A State Pension instead.
#ASSERT `How much lump sum am I paid under regulation 19, in pounds` `a state pension under regulation 20` 3500 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not covered.
#ASSERT `How much lump sum am I paid under regulation 19, in pounds` `regulation 18 does not cover the person` 3500 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Q44. Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred or increased graduated retirement benefit (reg 20(1))?
-- They were entitled to an increase and regulation 18 does not come into it.
