#ASSERT `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I am engaged in caring` 20 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- The same woman, 10 hours.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I am engaged in caring` 10 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Not ordinarily resident in Great Britain.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I am engaged in caring` 20 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- In prison.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I am engaged in caring` 20 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Schedule 1B but not ordinarily resident in Great Britain.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I am engaged in caring` 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- Q77. Am I engaged in caring in the week for the Regulations' purposes (reg 37(2))?
-- 20 hours, relevant benefit.
#ASSERT `Am I engaged in caring in the week for the Regulations' purposes` 20 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 19 hours.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I engaged in caring in the week for the Regulations' purposes` 19 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Schedule 1B.
#ASSERT `Am I engaged in caring in the week for the Regulations' purposes` 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- In prison.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I engaged in caring in the week for the Regulations' purposes` 20 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- Q78. Is the benefit the person I care for gets a relevant benefit (reg 37(4))?
-- Attendance allowance.
#ASSERT `Is the benefit the person I care for gets a relevant benefit` `attendance allowance in accordance with section 64 of the 1992 Act`
-- Personal independence payment, daily living component.
#ASSERT `Is the benefit the person I care for gets a relevant benefit` `the daily living component of personal independence payment in accordance with section 78 of the 2012 Act`
-- None listed.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the benefit the person I care for gets a relevant benefit` `no benefit that regulation 37(4) lists`)

-- Q79. Does my application for a carer's credit contain what the Regulations require (reg 37(6))?
-- Everything, benefit named, no declaration asked for.
#ASSERT `Does my application for a carer's credit contain what the Regulations require` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- No 20-hour declaration.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my application for a carer's credit contain what the Regulations require` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- No names.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my application for a carer's credit contain what the Regulations require` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- A relevant benefit but not named.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my application for a carer's credit contain what the Regulations require` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Nobody on a relevant benefit, so none to name.
#ASSERT `Does my application for a carer's credit contain what the Regulations require` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A level declaration asked for and missing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my application for a carer's credit contain what the Regulations require` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Asked for and given.
#ASSERT `Does my application for a carer's credit contain what the Regulations require` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

-- Q80. Is the person who signs my level-of-care declaration an appropriate person (reg 37(7))?
-- Both.
#ASSERT `Is the person who signs my level-of-care declaration an appropriate person` TRUE TRUE
-- Involved, not considered appropriate.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the person who signs my level-of-care declaration an appropriate person` TRUE FALSE)
-- Considered appropriate, not involved.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the person who signs my level-of-care declaration an appropriate person` FALSE TRUE)

-- Q81. On what day does my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring begin (reg 38(1))?
-- Before entitlement on 1 June 2027.
#ASSERT `On what day does my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring begin` `before the person becomes entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` (YMD 2027 6 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 3 9)
-- After the week ended on Saturday 5 June 2027.
#ASSERT `On what day does my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring begin` `after the week in which the person ceases to be entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` (YMD 2027 6 5) EQUALS (YMD 2027 6 6)
-- After regulation 37(2)(a) ceases.
#ASSERT `On what day does my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring begin` `after the week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied` (YMD 2027 6 5) EQUALS (YMD 2027 6 6)

-- Q82. On what day does my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring end (reg 38(1))?
-- Before entitlement on 1 June 2027.
#ASSERT `On what day does my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring end` `before the person becomes entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` (YMD 2027 6 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 5 31)
-- After the week ended on 5 June 2027.
#ASSERT `On what day does my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring end` `after the week in which the person ceases to be entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` (YMD 2027 6 5) EQUALS (YMD 2027 8 28)
-- After regulation 37(2)(a) ceases.
#ASSERT `On what day does my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring end` `after the week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied` (YMD 2027 6 5) EQUALS (YMD 2027 8 28)

-- Q83. Is this day within my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring (reg 38(1), (2))?
-- The first day of the 12 weeks before 1 June 2027.
#ASSERT `Is this day within my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring` `before the person becomes entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` (YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2027 3 9) FALSE
-- The day before that.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day within my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring` `before the person becomes entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` (YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2027 3 8) FALSE)
-- The day of entitlement itself is not in it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day within my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring` `before the person becomes entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` (YMD 2027 6 1) (YMD 2027 6 1) FALSE)
-- The last day of the 12 weeks after 5 June 2027.
#ASSERT `Is this day within my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring` `after the week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied` (YMD 2027 6 5) (YMD 2027 8 28) FALSE
-- The day after that.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day within my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring` `after the week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied` (YMD 2027 6 5) (YMD 2027 8 29) FALSE)
-- After ceasing carer's allowance, but a week of regulation 7A credit: shut out.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this day within my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring` `after the week in which the person ceases to be entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` (YMD 2027 6 5) (YMD 2027 7 1) TRUE)
-- The same week for the other kinds: paragraph (2) does not reach them.
#ASSERT `Is this day within my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring` `after the week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied` (YMD 2027 6 5) (YMD 2027 7 1) TRUE

-- Q84. Is my application for a credit received in time (reg 39)?
-- A week in 2025, received on the last day of the following tax year, 5 April 2027.
#ASSERT `Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37` (YMD 2025 10 6) (YMD 2027 4 5) FALSE (YMD 2027 12 31)
-- A day later.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37` (YMD 2025 10 6) (YMD 2027 4 6) FALSE (YMD 2027 12 31))
-- Received within the first following year.
#ASSERT `Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37` (YMD 2025 10 6) (YMD 2026 4 6) FALSE (YMD 2027 12 31)
-- Late, but a further time was allowed to 31 December 2027.
#ASSERT `Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37` (YMD 2025 10 6) (YMD 2027 12 31) TRUE (YMD 2027 12 31)
-- After that further time.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37` (YMD 2025 10 6) (YMD 2028 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 12 31))
-- A further time that ends before the ordinary deadline does not shorten it.
#ASSERT `Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37` (YMD 2025 10 6) (YMD 2027 3 1) TRUE (YMD 2027 1 1)
-- The week beginning 5 April 2026 counts in tax year 2025: received on 5 April 2027.
#ASSERT `Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37` (YMD 2026 4 5) (YMD 2027 4 5) FALSE (YMD 2027 12 31)
-- The week beginning 6 April 2026 is in tax year 2026: received on 5 April 2028.
#ASSERT `Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37` (YMD 2026 4 6) (YMD 2028 4 5) FALSE (YMD 2027 12 31)
-- The same week, received on 6 April 2028.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37` (YMD 2026 4 6) (YMD 2028 4 6) FALSE (YMD 2027 12 31))
-- Regulation 35 application received on the last day of the year of the week: not after its end.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 35` (YMD 2025 10 6) (YMD 2026 4 5) FALSE (YMD 2027 12 31))
-- Regulation 35 application received the day after that year ends.
#ASSERT `Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 35` (YMD 2025 10 6) (YMD 2026 4 6) FALSE (YMD 2027 12 31)
-- Regulation 35 application received during the year.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 35` (YMD 2025 10 6) (YMD 2025 12 1) FALSE (YMD 2027 12 31))
-- Regulation 35 application received in 2040: the text gives no latest date (F31).
#ASSERT `Is my application for a credit received in time` `an application under regulation 35` (YMD 2025 10 6) (YMD 2040 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2027 12 31)


§ `Cases that record findings (NOTES.md, "What the text turns out to say")`

-- Finding 1 (fork F8). Regulation 1(3) takes a person who reaches pensionable age before 6 April 2016 outside the Regulations (except Part 5);
-- yet regulation 16(3) gives an inherited amount to a person who was over pensionable age when the spouse, who reached it before 6 April 2016, died on or after that day.
-- A person who reached pensionable age on 1 January 2016, whose spouse (pensionable age 2010) died on 1 June 2016, is inside 16(3) and outside the gate.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do these Regulations apply to me` (YMD 2016 1 1))
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of regulation 16 gives me an inherited amount` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2016 1 1) `married to each other` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2016 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2010 1 1) EQUALS JUST `regulation 16(3) applies`

-- Finding 3. A woman with a reduced rate election in force is shut out of the credits in regs 28, 30 and 33, but regulation 37(8) lifts the application requirement for her.
-- (Cases under the questions above: regs 28/33 and 30 give false for her; reg 37 gives true with 20 hours and no application, false with 10 hours.)

